From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:05:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: release a pending A-MSDU when a WED RX queue is
 empty

mt76_rx_release_burst() keeps the subframes of an A-MSDU until its last
subframe arrives, or until the next frame of the same radio on that
queue shows that the A-MSDU has ended.

With WED, the subframes of flows that the PPE has bound are forwarded by
the hardware and never reach the host. When the last subframe of an
A-MSDU is one of them, the subframes that the host received wait for the
next frame of that radio on that queue, which can take seconds when the
clients send little to the host: a DNS query that a client sends in the
same A-MSDU as TCP ACKs of an offloaded download is answered only when
another frame arrives.

Release the pending A-MSDUs of a WED RX queue when a poll finds the
queue empty. A subframe that the hardware writes after that arrives on
its own, carries the PN of the subframes before it and fails the PN
check, as it does already when another frame arrives between two
subframes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -1112,6 +1112,14 @@ int mt76_dma_rx_poll(struct napi_struct
 
 	do {
 		cur = mt76_dma_rx_process(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid], budget - done);
+
+		/* WED can forward subframes of an A-MSDU in hardware, so the
+		 * last one may never reach the host: once the queue is empty,
+		 * pass on the subframes received so far
+		 */
+		if (!cur && mt76_queue_is_wed_rx(&dev->q_rx[qid]))
+			mt76_rx_release_pending_amsdu(dev, qid);
+
 		mt76_rx_poll_complete(dev, qid, napi);
 		done += cur;
 	} while (cur && done < budget);
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -956,6 +956,18 @@ static void mt76_rx_release_burst(struct
 		mt76_rx_release_amsdu(phy, q);
 }
 
+void mt76_rx_release_pending_amsdu(struct mt76_dev *dev, enum mt76_rxq_id q)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->phys); i++) {
+		struct mt76_phy *phy = dev->phys[i];
+
+		if (phy && phy->rx_amsdu[q].head)
+			mt76_rx_release_amsdu(phy, q);
+	}
+}
+
 void mt76_rx(struct mt76_dev *dev, enum mt76_rxq_id q, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct mt76_rx_status *status = (struct mt76_rx_status *)skb->cb;
--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -1557,6 +1557,7 @@ static inline bool mt76_is_testmode_skb(
 }
 
 void mt76_rx(struct mt76_dev *dev, enum mt76_rxq_id q, struct sk_buff *skb);
+void mt76_rx_release_pending_amsdu(struct mt76_dev *dev, enum mt76_rxq_id q);
 void mt76_tx(struct mt76_phy *dev, struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 	     struct mt76_wcid *wcid, struct sk_buff *skb);
 void mt76_wake_tx_queue(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_txq *txq);
